%I A402377 #24 Nov 24 2026 17:28:06
%S A402377 1,1,-1,3,-13,68,-400,2549,-17211,121399,-886015,6645871,-50980537,
%T A402377 398460924,-3164115430,25469788686,-207453475580,1707264018507,
%U A402377 -14178803855835,118713214173886,-1001174332303862,8498795373827039,-72572596103006575,623049855096735036
%N A402377 Coefficient a(n) of z^n in the power series in the normalized squared Peclet number, z=Pe^2/(16*Pi^2), of the normalized Rayleigh number Ra_a/(4*Pi^2) at the onset of absolute instability of the flow in the Darcy-Prats problem on convection in porous media with throughflow.
%C A402377 The fact that all a(n) are integers is not trivial: the coefficients of series expansions of an algebraic function are rational and in general are not integers. In arXiv:2611.17614 this is proved via the integer lift on an elliptic model.
%C A402377 The selected neutral saddles of the dispersion relation that define the onset of absolute instability lie on an arc of the elliptic curve 11a3 of conductor 11 in Cremona's tables (proved in arXiv:2611.17614).
%D A402377 A. Barletta, Routes to Absolute Instability in Porous Media, Springer, 2019.
%D A402377 M. Prats, The effect of horizontal fluid flow on thermally induced convection currents in porous mediums, J. Geophys. Res., 71 (1966), 4835-4838.
%H A402377 Oleg Kirillov, <a href="/A402377/b402377.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..500</a>
%H A402377 F. Dufour and M.-C. Neel, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1063/1.869741">Numerical study of instability in a horizontal porous channel with bottom heating and forced horizontal flow</a>, Phys. Fluids, 10 (1998), 2198-2207.
%H A402377 Oleg N. Kirillov, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.17614">Global saddle selection and exact absolute-instability boundaries for convection in porous media with throughflow</a>, arXiv:2611.17614 [physics.flu-dyn], 2026.
%F A402377 G.f. A(x)=Sum_{n>=0} a(n)*x^n satisfies F(4*A(x),4*x)=0 with A(0)=1, where F(r,P)=64*r^7- (96*P +1024)*r^6+ (48*P^2 + 2272*P + 5504)*r^5+ (-8*P^3 - 1824*P^2 - 7328*P - 10496)*r^4+ (740*P^3 - 7664*P^2 - 12384*P + 3136)*r^3+ (-107*P^4 + 14564*P^3 + 63104*P^2 + 45952*P - 256)*r^2+ (-6464*P^4 - 40832*P^3 - 70976*P^2 - 12800*P)*r+ (1024*P^5 - 4096*P^4 + 6144*P^3 - 4096*P^2 + 1024*P).
%F A402377 Since dF/dr=50176 != 0 at (r,P)=(4,0), F=0 has a unique power series solution with A(0)=1, although F=0 also has other branches.
%F A402377 D-finiteness follows from the algebraicity of A(x) proved in arXiv:2611.17614. a(n) satisfies a linear recurrence of order 26 with polynomial coefficients of degree 6 in n.
%F A402377 Radius of convergence |z_s|=0.1040070010090197..., where z_s is the negative root of the irreducible polynomial 31212*z^4 + 21249*z^3 + 130005*z^2 + 12096*z - 128 = 0, is proved in arXiv:2611.17614. Note that the polynomial has a positive root 0.0095916..., which is not a singularity of A(x).
%F A402377 a(n) ~ c*(-1)^n*d^n/n^(5/2) is proved in arXiv:2611.17614, where d = 1/|z_s| = 9.614737376316406..., and c = -0.03725997... (numerically).
%e A402377 For z = Pe^2/(16*Pi^2): Ra_a = 4*Pi^2*(1+z-z^2+3*z^3-...) = 4*Pi^2+Pe^2/4-Pe^4/(64*Pi^2)+3*Pe^6/(1024*Pi^4)-..., where Pe^2/4 follows from the Ginzburg-Landau approximation (Dufour and Neel, 1998), although the Ginzburg-Landau approximation differs from the exact series starting with the Pe^4 term.
%p A402377 with(gfun):
%p A402377 F := (64)*r^7
%p A402377    + (-96*P - 1024)*r^6
%p A402377    + (48*P^2 + 2272*P + 5504)*r^5
%p A402377    + (-8*P^3 - 1824*P^2 - 7328*P - 10496)*r^4
%p A402377    + (740*P^3 - 7664*P^2 - 12384*P + 3136)*r^3
%p A402377    + (-107*P^4 + 14564*P^3 + 63104*P^2 + 45952*P - 256)*r^2
%p A402377    + (-6464*P^4 - 40832*P^3 - 70976*P^2 - 12800*P)*r
%p A402377    + (1024*P^5 - 4096*P^4 + 6144*P^3 - 4096*P^2 + 1024*P):
%p A402377 F__yz:=subs(r=4*y,P=4*z,F):
%p A402377 deq:=algeqtodiffeq(F__yz, y(z), {y(0) = 1, D(y)(0) = 1, (D@@2)(y)(0) = -2}):
%p A402377 rec:=diffeqtorec(deq, y(z), u(n)):
%p A402377 newseq:=rectoproc(rec, u(n), remember):
%p A402377 [seq(newseq(n), n = 0 .. 23)];
%K A402377 sign,new
%O A402377 0,4
%A A402377 _Oleg Kirillov_, Nov 17 2026
